From 11484337754d0557aeabc6cf969bce39671612b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <107831991+SyntaxError-PEBKAC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:06:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] ducksteps: enlarge and reposition the About dialog
 wordmark

The wordmark sat small and marooned near the top of the dialog, with a
gap of roughly 52px between it and "Extended Support Release".

The cause is inside the asset. about-wordmark.svg is a 359x80 canvas but
the glyphs only occupy x 2-236, y 13-71 of it - a third of the width is
empty. So background-size: auto 44px sized the canvas to 197x44 while
the visible word came out at just 130x32, and background-position: 0 0
pinned it against the top edge with the canvas's own 7px of slack above.

Sizing to 68px puts the visible word at 199x49, and offsetting it 16px
down closes the gap to about 23px, which groups it with the text block
underneath instead of leaving it stranded. padding-top grows to match,
so nothing below it moves up into the wordmark. Net effect on the dialog
is roughly 18px taller.

The base sheet sets background-position wholesale for RTL:

    &:-moz-locale-dir(rtl) {
      background-position: 100% 0;
    }

which has the same specificity as our rule and would have discarded the
vertical offset, so that case is mirrored here.

Note this does not fix the horizontal half of the same problem: under
RTL the canvas is right-aligned, which leaves the word about 105px shy
of the edge because of that unused canvas. Tightening the SVG's viewBox
to its ink would fix it properly and make these numbers mean what they
say, but that is an asset change for another commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../branding/ducksteps/content/aboutDialog.css   | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/branding/ducksteps/content/aboutDialog.css b/browser/branding/ducksteps/content/aboutDialog.css
index 4413027a5bba..fe99cf028e3d 100644
--- a/browser/branding/ducksteps/content/aboutDialog.css
+++ b/browser/branding/ducksteps/content/aboutDialog.css
@@ -19,9 +19,21 @@
 }
 
 #rightBox {
-  background-size: auto 44px;
+  /* The wordmark is drawn into a 359x80 canvas but its ink spans only
+     x 2-236, y 13-71 of it, so these numbers are all larger than the word
+     they produce: at 68px the visible "ducksteps" is 199x49.
+     background-position drops it clear of the top edge, and padding-top
+     reserves the wordmark's height plus the gap beneath it. */
+  background-size: auto 68px;
+  background-position: 0 16px;
   margin-inline: 30px;
-  padding-top: 76px;
+  padding-top: 94px;
+
+  /* The base sheet resets the position wholesale for RTL, which would
+     otherwise throw away the vertical offset above. */
+  &:-moz-locale-dir(rtl) {
+    background-position: 100% 16px;
+  }
 }
 
 #bottomBox {
